[00:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Welcome to the Anti-Gravity Studio tutorial. In this video, we\'ll show you how to edit 360° footage captured with anti-gravity A1. Download the studio software from the official website, then install it. You can optionally choose to'

[00:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'install the Quicklook plugin. Once installed, this allows you to preview footage instantly by pressing the space bar on any asset without opening the studio software. The studio interface includes two main tabs, the media tab'

[00:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and the project tab. The media tab is used for previewing and editing individual clips, while the project tab lets you combine multiple clips and add text, music, transitions, and other elements.'

[00:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Let\'s start with the media tab which is DE divided into four sections library monitor function panel and clip panel. One library. When your computer is'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'connected to the drone or a memory card containing drone footage, Studio can automatically recognize and import footage. You can open a file by clicking on it.'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'or by dragging it directly into the clip area. Hover your mouse over a clip to preview'

[01:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it. Two, monitor. Use your mouse to drag the clip and adjust the viewing angle. Scroll the mouse wheel to change the'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'field of view. Click the ratio setting in the lower right corner to select a common video aspect ratio based on your project needs. When the view has been moved, click the'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'icon above to return to the default view. T three function panel. You can choose to enable or disable stabilization and'

[02:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'goggle view according to your needs. Under the viewpoint tab, you can switch between different viewing angles. Choose the stitching method based on whether'

[02:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your drone is equipped with propeller guards. If the stitching result isn\'t ideal, you can select a reference image to recalibrate and correct it. In the image processing panel, adjust'

[02:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the brightness and color of the footage to your preference. Under the dashboard tab, you can apply different dashboard styles to display flight information in your video.'

[02:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Four. Timeline panel. Drag the timeline'

[03:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'or press the space bar to preview and play your clip. Move the white handles at either end of the timeline to adjust the clip\'s duration.'

[03:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You can also click anywhere on the timeline to set that point as the start or end of the clip range. Click the plus button to add a key frame'

[03:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'at the current position. At each key frame, you can adjust parameters such as rotation, field of view, and more. Add another key frame later in the clip'

[03:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and change the settings. The footage will transition smoothly between the two key frames. Use depth tracking to keep your subject'

[03:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'centered. Select the subject Start tracking and wait for the process to complete. The subject will stay fixed in the'

[04:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'frame. Enable the ND filter effect to add motion blur around the edges during'

[04:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'movement, creating a more dynamic look. When editing is complete, click export in the upper right corner to save your edited clip.'

[04:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Project tab one. Create project. Click new project to start a new project. You can rename the project, set the save'

[04:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'path, adjust the aspect ratio, frame rate, and other parameters. If your device has limited performance, enable proxy mode for a smoother editing experience.'

[04:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The project page is similar to the clip page and is also divided into four sections: clip library, player, timeline, and function panel. The player timeline and function panel'

[05:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'work the same way as on the clip page, but the library also includes music, text, and transitions tabs. You can use the built-in library to add clips to the timeline and create your'

[05:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'own videos. Click the plus icon on a clip or drag and drop it from the media library to the timeline to start editing. Drag the timeline or press the space bar to'

[05:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'preview and play the clip. Use the slider or press control an C to zoom in or out of the timeline centered on the play head.'

[05:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Move the cursor to the start or end of a clip. Then click and drag to trim it manually. You can also use the crop tool to'

[06:04] [scene:talk]
